IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vea-veteran`
IMPORT `vea-formulas`

-- Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 -- worked cases for the rates computed from the formulas sidecar
-- (C2004A03268.formulas.md), from the seat of the veteran and of the widow or widower.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the formulas and the deposited text (C2026C00275), never copied from the encoding's output; the working is in the
-- comment above each case. Every case is HYPOTHETICAL. The rates on the day before are the compilation's printed figures
-- standing in; the single pension rate MBR amounts ($1,128.80, $1,149.00, $1,160.00), the CPI numbers and the annual
-- pension MBR ($28,600) are made-up figures, not published ones.
--
-- Ray (HYPOTHETICAL), a Vietnam veteran on the special (TPI) rate.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 59LA -- the pension MBR factor`

-- The arguments: current single pension rate MBR amount; previous.
-- 1,149.00 / 1,128.80 = 1.017895...: 3 places 1.017, 4th place 8, greater than 4: 1.018.
#ASSERT `the pension MBR factor` 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 1.018
-- An MBR amount that fell, 1,120.00 / 1,128.80 = 0.992...: increased to 1 (s 59LA(2A)(b)).
#ASSERT `the pension MBR factor` 1120 1128.8 EQUALS 1

§§ `s 198(5DA), (5E), (8A) -- the rates on an adjustment day`

-- The arguments: which rate; rate the day before; MBR amount on the adjustment day; the day before.
-- The general rate: 338.94 × 1.018 = 345.04092, rounded up to the nearest $0.10: 345.10.
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the general rate of disability pension (s 22(3), indexed by s 198(5DA))` 338.94 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 345.1
-- The extreme disablement adjustment: 510.40 × 1.018 = 519.5872: 519.60.
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4), indexed by s 198(5E))` 510.40 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 519.6
-- The intermediate rate: 619.80 × 1.018 = 630.9564: 631.00.
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the intermediate rate (s 23(4), indexed by s 198(5E))` 619.80 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 631
-- Ray's special rate: 1,595.66 × 1.018 = 1,595.66 + 28.72188 = 1,624.38188: 1,624.40.
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the special rate (s 24(4), indexed by s 198(5E))` 1595.66 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 1624.4
-- The s 30(1)(b) amount: 35 × 1.018 = 35.63: 35.70 (s 198(8A)).
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the war widow's or widower's amount in s 30(1)(b) (indexed by s 198(8A))` 35 1149 1128.8 EQUALS 35.7
-- MBR amount fell: factor 1, but the substitution is still made and rounded up: 338.94 becomes 339.00 (finding 16).
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the general rate of disability pension (s 22(3), indexed by s 198(5DA))` 338.94 1120 1128.8 EQUALS 339
-- A rate already a multiple of $0.10, factor 1: unchanged, 345.10.
#ASSERT `What does the rate become on the adjustment day` `the general rate of disability pension (s 22(3), indexed by s 198(5DA))` 345.1 1120 1128.8 EQUALS 345.1
-- The arguments: starting rate; MBR amounts in order.
-- Two adjustment days: 338.94 → 345.10; then 1,160 / 1,149 = 1.0095735...: 1.009, 4th place 5: 1.010; 345.10 × 1.01 = 348.551: 348.60.
#ASSERT `the rate after these adjustment days` 338.94 (LIST 1128.8, 1149, 1160) EQUALS 348.6
-- No adjustment day (one MBR amount, or none): the starting rate.
#ASSERT `the rate after these adjustment days` 338.94 (LIST 1128.8) EQUALS 338.94
#ASSERT `the rate after these adjustment days` 338.94 (LIST) EQUALS 338.94

§§ `s 198(4), (5) -- CPI-indexed relevant rates`

-- The arguments: rate before; CPI for the last December or June quarter; highest earlier; brought-forward left.
-- s 30(1)(c), $25.60: 140 / 137 = 1.02189...: 1.021, 4th place 8: 1.022; 25.60 × 1.022 = 26.1632, 6.32 cents above 26.10: 26.20.
#ASSERT `the relevant rate for the period` 25.60 140 137 0 EQUALS 26.2
-- With 0.007 still brought forward: 1.022 − 0.007 = 1.015; 25.984, 8.4 cents above 25.90: 26.00.
#ASSERT `the relevant rate for the period` 25.60 140 137 0.007 EQUALS 26
-- A CPI below its highest earlier number: no substitution, 25.60.
#ASSERT `the relevant rate for the period` 25.60 136 137 0 EQUALS 25.6
-- Exactly 5 cents above a multiple: $10 × 1.005 = 10.05, to the next higher multiple, 10.10 (s 198(4)(b)(i)).
#ASSERT `the relevant rate for the period` 10 100.5 100 0 EQUALS 10.1

§§ `ss 22 to 24, 30(1) -- the pensions, on the indexed rates`

-- The arguments: degree; blinded; how much work; ended work and lost earnings; claimed before 65; last job after 65;
-- age; impairment points; lifestyle points; the four rates the day before; MBR on the adjustment day; the day before.
-- Ray, 80%, no more than 8 hours' work, lost earnings, claimed at 58: the special rate, 1,624.40 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `What rate of disability pension am I paid now` 80 FALSE `no more than 8 hours a week, because of my war-caused incapacity alone` TRUE TRUE FALSE 58 0 0 338.94 510.40 619.80 1595.66 1149 1128.8 EQUALS `the special rate (s 24), per fortnight` 1624.4
-- Part-time only: the intermediate rate, 631.00.
#ASSERT `What rate of disability pension am I paid now` 80 FALSE `only part-time or intermittently (under half of full-time hours, or under 20 hours a week), because of it alone` TRUE TRUE FALSE 58 0 0 338.94 510.40 619.80 1595.66 1149 1128.8 EQUALS `the intermediate rate (s 23), per fortnight` 631
-- Able to work more: 80% of the general rate, 0.8 × 345.10 = 276.08.
#ASSERT `What rate of disability pension am I paid now` 80 FALSE `more than that` TRUE TRUE FALSE 58 0 0 338.94 510.40 619.80 1595.66 1149 1128.8 EQUALS `the general rate pension (s 22(2)): my degree of incapacity as a percentage of the general rate, per fortnight` 276.08
-- 100%, 70, 75 impairment points, lifestyle 6: the extreme disablement adjustment, 519.60.
#ASSERT `What rate of disability pension am I paid now` 100 FALSE `more than that` FALSE FALSE FALSE 70 75 6 338.94 510.40 619.80 1595.66 1149 1128.8 EQUALS `the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)), per fortnight` 519.6
-- The arguments: annual pension MBR; (b) the day before; MBR on the adjustment day; the day before; (c) before; CPI;
-- highest earlier CPI; brought-forward left.
-- Ray's widow: 28,600 / 26 = 1,100, plus (b) 35.70, plus (c) 26.20: 1,161.90 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `What is my war widow's pension a fortnight now` 28600 35 1149 1128.8 25.60 140 137 0 EQUALS 1161.9
